hadiths[69]{hadithnumber,text}:
"633","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that (on one occasion) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A messenger came to me from my Lord and informed me—or he said: gave me glad tidings—that whoever from my Ummah dies in a state that he does not associate anything with Allah, he will enter Paradise."" I asked, ""Even if he has committed adultery and even if he has stolen?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Even if he has committed adultery, even if he has stolen."
"634","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies while associating partners with Allah will enter the Hellfire."" I (Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him) say: Whoever dies without associating partners with Allah will enter Paradise."
"635","Narrated by Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to do seven things and forbade us from seven things. He commanded us: to accompany funeral processions, to visit the sick, to accept invitations, to help the oppressed, to fulfill oaths, to return greetings, and to say “Yarhamuk Allah” to one who sneezes. And he forbade us: from (using) silver utensils, gold rings, and (wearing) silk, dibaj, qazz, and istabraq (all are types of silk fabrics). (And the seventh thing among them was left out.)"
"636","Umm al-'Ala, an Ansari woman (narrates that she) had pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace be upon him) (on Islam), that the Muhajirun cast lots among themselves (for the division by the Ansar), and our lot fell to 'Uthman bin Maz'un (may Allah be pleased with him), so we hosted him in our house. Then he fell ill with the illness in which he passed away. When he died, and he had been washed and shrouded in his clothes, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came. I said, ""O Abu Sa'ib! May Allah's mercy be upon you. My testimony for you is that Allah has honored you."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""How do you know that Allah has honored him?"" I replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! May my father be sacrificed for you. (I said this because) if Allah does not honor him, then who will He honor?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Indeed, he has died (in a good state), and I also hope for good for him, but by Allah, I do not know, though I am Allah's Messenger, what will be done with me."" Umm al-'Ala says, ""After that, I never testified to anyone's purity."
"637","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): When my father was martyred in the (battle of Uhud), I would repeatedly remove the cloth from his face and weep, and people would stop me, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not stop me. Then my paternal aunt Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) also began to weep, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whether you weep or not, the angels continued to shade him with their wings until you lifted him (from the battlefield)."
"638","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed about the death of Najashi on the day he passed away. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) went to the place of prayer, arranged the people in rows, and said four takbirs, that is, he offered the funeral prayer in absentia."
"639","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): (During the time when the Battle of Mu'tah was taking place, on one of those days) the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (to us): ""(At this moment) Zaid took the flag and he was martyred, then Ja'far took the flag and he was martyred, then Abdullah bin Rawahah took the flag and he was martyred, and the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were flowing (with tears due to excessive weeping). Then Khalid bin Walid took the flag without being appointed as commander, and victory was granted at his hands."
"640","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Any Muslim whose three children, who had not reached puberty, die, Allah will admit him into Paradise due to the great mercy He has for those children."
"641","Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us while we were washing his daughter, and he said: ""Wash her three times, or five times, or more than that if you see fit, with pure water and lotus leaves, and in the end add camphor (to the water). Then when you have finished, inform me."" So when we finished, we informed him, and he gave us his waist-wrapper and said: ""Shroud her body with it."
"642","In another narration, (Sayyida Umm Atiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, says) the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Begin washing from her right side and from the places of ablution."" (Umm Atiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her) says that we combed her hair and divided it into three parts."
"643","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was shrouded in three garments which were Yemeni, Sahuli, made of cotton, and neither silk nor wool. There was neither a shirt nor a turban among these garments."
"644","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that: While a man was standing at Arafat, he suddenly fell from his mount and the mount crushed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Bathe him with water and lote tree leaves, shroud him in two garments, do not apply perfume to his body, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting Talbiyah (in the state of Ihram)."
"645","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that when Abdullah bin Ubayy (the hypocrite) died, his son came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""Please give me your shirt and pray his funeral prayer and seek forgiveness for him."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him his shirt and said, ""(When the funeral is ready) inform me so that I may pray for him."" Accordingly, he informed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to pray for him, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) held him from behind and said, ""Has Allah not forbidden you to pray for the hypocrites?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I have been given a choice in this matter. Allah has said: 'Whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them (it is all the same for them); even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.'"" (Surah At-Tawbah: 80) So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed his funeral prayer, then this verse was revealed: ""And never pray (the funeral prayer) for any of them (the hypocrites) who dies."" (Surah At-Tawbah: 84)"
"646","Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Abdullah bin Ubayy after he had been placed in the grave, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) had him taken out, put his saliva in his mouth, and dressed him in his own shirt."
"647","Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We migrated with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) solely for the pleasure of Allah Almighty, so our reward became assured with Allah. Some of us are such that they passed away and did not take anything from their reward (in this world); among them was Sayyiduna Mus'ab bin Umair (may Allah be pleased with him). And some of us are those for whom their fruit ripened and they are picking and eating it. Sayyiduna Mus'ab bin Umair (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred on the day of Uhud, and we did not find anything from his belongings with which we could shroud him except a single sheet (and that too was so small that) if we covered his head with it, his feet would be exposed, and if we covered his feet, his head would be exposed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed us to cover his head and to put idhkhir (a type of grass) on his feet."
"648","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) that a woman brought a bordered sheet as a gift to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (Then Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) asked those present:) Do you know what a ""burdah"" is? They said (yes, we know, a burdah) is a ""shimlah"" (that is, it is called a sheet). Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said yes. The woman said: I have made it with my own hands and have brought it so that you may wear it. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted it. At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was also in need of clothing, so he came out and that sheet was his lower garment. Then a man praised it and said: Please give it to me. (So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave it to him.) The people said (to that man): You did not do well; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore it in a state of great need, and you asked him for it, and you also know that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) does not refuse a request (no matter how great his own need may be). That man replied: By Allah! I did not ask for it so that I could wear it, but I asked for it so that it would be my shroud. Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) says that then that very sheet became his shroud."
"649","Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We were forbidden from accompanying funeral processions, but it was not with strict prohibition."
"650","Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him), says: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) say: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah to mourn for any deceased person for more than three days, except for her husband, for whom she should mourn for four months and ten days."
"651","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): (Once) the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a woman who was sitting and weeping at a grave. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: ""Fear Allah and be patient."" She replied, ""Go away from me, for you have not been afflicted with a calamity like mine."" Later, it was said to her that he was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (and you have replied to him so disrespectfully). So she came to the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (she thought there would be guards at the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but) she did not find any guards at his door. Then she said, ""I did not recognize you (that is why I replied disrespectfully, now I will be patient)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Patience is at the first stroke of calamity."
"652","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (Sayyidah Zainab, may Allah be pleased with her) sent a man to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that my son is in the throes of death, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent back (this) message (saying): ""Convey my greetings and say: (What should I do by coming?) Whatever Allah has given and whatever He has taken, all belongs to Him, and everything with Him has an appointed term, so you should be patient and hope for reward."" Again, she sent a man to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and made him swear that he must come, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, and with him were Sa'd bin 'Ubadah, Mu'adh bin Jabal, Ubayy bin Ka'b, Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with them), and some other companions (may Allah be pleased with them). (When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, arrived there) the child was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and (at that time it was his last moments) his soul was fluttering (Abu 'Uthman, the narrator, says) I think (Sayyiduna Usama, may Allah be pleased with him) said that he was fluttering as if it were a waterskin (being shaken). Then the eyes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to flow with tears, so Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is this?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is mercy which Allah has placed in the hearts of His servants, and Allah shows mercy only to those of His servants who are merciful."
"653","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): We were accompanying the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the funeral of his daughter (Sayyidah Umm Kulthum, may Allah be pleased with her), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting by the grave. He (Anas) said: I saw that the eyes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were shedding tears. Then Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: (When the grave was prepared), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is there anyone among you who did not have intercourse last night?"" So Abu Talhah said: I am (that person). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You go down (into the grave)."" So he went down into her grave."
"654","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The deceased is punished because of the weeping of his relatives over him."" After the martyrdom of Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), this matter reached Umm-ul-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), so she said: ""May Allah have mercy on Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). By Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not say that a believer is punished because of the weeping of his relatives, rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Allah increases the punishment of a disbeliever because of the weeping of his relatives.'"" And after this she said: ""The Qur'an (this verse) is sufficient for you: 'No bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.' (Surah Al-An'am: 164)"" __QUR_N__ __XREF_N__ __REF_N__"
"655","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by the grave of a Jewish woman, whose relatives were weeping over her death. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These people are weeping for her, while she is being punished in her grave."
"656","Sayyiduna Mughira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Lying upon me is not like lying upon any one of you. Whoever lies upon me should find his place in the Hellfire."" And I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever wails over someone will be punished because of that wailing."
"657","Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""He is not one of us who slaps his cheeks, tears his clothes, and calls with the call of the days of ignorance."
"658","Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to visit me in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage because of an illness that had become severe for me. So I said, “You see the condition of my illness, and I am a wealthy man, and after me, I have no heir except my only daughter. Should I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “No.” I said, “Half?” But the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “No.” I said, “A third?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A third, and a third is still a lot. It is better that you leave your heirs wealthy than to leave them poor, begging from people. And whatever you spend seeking the pleasure of Allah, you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you put in your wife’s mouth.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Will I be left behind (in Makkah) after my companions?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “If you are left behind and do good deeds, your rank and status will only increase. Perhaps you will live a long life so that some people (i.e., Muslims) will benefit from you and some people (i.e., disbelievers) will be harmed by you. O Allah! Complete the migration of my companions and do not turn them back (i.e., do not let them die in Makkah). But poor Sa’d bin Khawlah.” (The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, expressed sorrow for him) because he died in Makkah."
"659","`Sayyiduna Abu Musa (Ash'ari) (may Allah be pleased with him)` once became seriously ill, and (one day) he fell unconscious, and his head was in the lap of a woman from among his relatives, and she began to weep. Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) did not have enough strength to stop her. Then when he regained consciousness, he said: ""I am free from that person from whom Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), declared himself free. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared himself free from the woman who wails loudly in grief, shaves her head, and tears her collar or garment."
"660","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) received the news of the martyrdom of Zaid bin Harithah, Ja’far, and Abdullah bin Rawahah (may Allah be pleased with them), he sat down. The effect of grief was visible on his face, and I was watching through a crack in the door. Meanwhile, a person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned the women of Sayyiduna Ja’far (may Allah be pleased with him) and their weeping. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered him to stop them. Accordingly, he went and stopped them. Then he came again to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said that they are not listening. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Stop them.” So he went and stopped them. Then for the third time, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! They have overpowered me, they are not listening to me.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Go and put dust in their mouths.”"
"661","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) had a son who fell ill and passed away. Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) was not at home at the time; he had gone out for some work. When his wife (Umm Sulaym) saw that the child had died, she bathed him, shrouded him, and laid him in a corner of the house. When Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) came home at night, he asked, ""How is the boy?"" His wife (Umm Sulaym) replied, ""He is at peace, and I hope he is resting comfortably."" Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) thought she was telling the truth. So Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) spent the night with his wife. When morning came, he performed ghusl and was about to go out when Umm Sulaym informed him that the boy had passed away. Then he performed the morning prayer with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). After that, they informed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) of what had happened between them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I hope Allah will bless you both in this night."" One of the Ansar (Sufyan says from me) said: ""I saw nine sons of both of them, all of whom were reciters of the Qur'an."
"662","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Abu Saif the blacksmith, and he (Abu Saif) was the foster father of (the Messenger of Allah’s son) Sayyiduna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took Sayyiduna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him), kissed him, and placed his blessed face upon him. Then after that, we went to Abu Saif’s house and Sayyiduna Ibrahim (may Allah be pleased with him) was in the throes of death. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became filled with tears. So Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him, “O Messenger of Allah! (Do you weep?)” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: “O Ibn Awf! This is a mercy.” Then he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept more and said: “The eye weeps and the heart grieves, but we do not say except that which pleases our Lord. And O Ibrahim! We are greatly grieved at your separation.”"
"663","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Sa'd bin Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) fell ill, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him accompanied by Abdur Rahman bin Awf, Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas, and Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them). When the Prophet (peace be upon him) arrived there, he found him lying on his bed at home. The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired: ""Has he passed away?"" The people replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! No."" Then the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) (seeing the severity of his illness) began to weep. When the people saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) weeping, they also began to weep. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah does not punish for the tears of the eye, nor for the grief of the heart, but He punishes or shows mercy because of this,"" and he pointed to his tongue. ""And indeed, the deceased is punished because of the wailing and lamentation of his relatives (if done unjustly) over him."
"664","Umm Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took a pledge from us at the time of allegiance that we would not wail (over the dead), but except for five women, no one fulfilled this pledge: (1) Umm Sulaym, (2) Umm ‘Ala’, (3) the daughter of Abu Sabrah who was the wife of Sayyiduna Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him), (4) two other women. Or she said: the daughter of Abu Sabrah, the wife of Mu’adh, and one other woman."
"665","Sayyiduna Amir bin Rabi’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “When any one of you sees a funeral procession, if he is not accompanying it, he should stand up until it passes by him or before it passes by him or until it is placed down.”"
"666","'(It is narrated from Sa'id al-Maqburi, may Allah have mercy on him)' During a funeral, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, took Marwan's hand and they both sat down before the bier was placed. At that very moment, Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, came and took Marwan's hand and said, ""Stand up! Indeed, he (Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him) knows that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade us from this."" So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said, ""He speaks the truth."
"667","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): A funeral passed in front of us and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up. We said, ""O Messenger of Allah! It was the funeral of a Jew."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whenever you see a funeral, stand up."
"668","Narrated by Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the funeral is placed and the men lift it on their shoulders, if the deceased was righteous, he says: 'Take me quickly.' And if he was not righteous, he says: 'Woe to me! Where are you taking me?' His voice is heard by everything except humans, and if humans were to hear it, they would fall unconscious."
"669","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Hasten with the funeral, for if it was righteous, you are bringing it closer to good, and if it was otherwise, then it is an evil which you are removing from your necks."
"670","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whoever accompanies a funeral will receive the reward of one qirat. So Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to narrate many ahadith to us about this. (Then he had this hadith inquired about from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)), so she confirmed Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this. So Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Then we have missed out on many qirats (i.e., rewards)."
"671","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said during his illness in which he passed away: “May Allah curse the Jews and the Christians, for they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that if this had not been feared, the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been made prominent, but I fear that it might also be made into a mosque."
"672","Narrated Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him): I offered the funeral prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a woman who had died during childbirth, and he stood in the middle (of her body) during her funeral prayer."
"673","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)` offered the funeral prayer and he recited Surah Al-Fatihah (in a loud voice) and said, (I recited it aloud) so that you may know that reciting Surah Al-Fatihah in the funeral prayer is Sunnah."
"674","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn back after burying him (then the deceased becomes aware to the extent that) he hears the sound of their sandals. Two angels come to him, make him sit up, and ask him: 'What did you use to say about this man, that is, Muhammad (peace be upon him)?' If he says, 'I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger,' then it will be said to him: 'Look at your place which was in Hell; Allah has given you a place in Paradise instead of it.' The Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) said that he sees both places. But as for the disbeliever or the hypocrite, he replies: 'I do not know; I used to say what the people used to say.' So it will be said to him: 'You neither understood with your intellect nor followed (the righteous).' Then he will be struck between his ears with an iron hammer, because of which he will let out a scream that all creatures near him will hear except humans and jinn."
"675","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Angel of Death was sent to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him). When he came, Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) struck him such a blow that one of his eyes was gouged out. The angel returned to his Lord and said, ""You have sent me to a servant who does not want to die."" Allah Almighty restored his eye and commanded him to go back to Musa (peace be upon him) and say: ""Place your hand on the back of an ox; for every hair that comes under your hand, you will be granted one year of life."" (So the angel came and conveyed the message of Allah to Musa, peace be upon him.) He said, ""O Lord! (When all those years have passed) what will happen then?"" Allah Almighty said, ""Then death will come."" He said, ""Let it be now."" Then he prayed to Allah Almighty: ""Bring me close to the Holy Land, as much as a stone's throw."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) after narrating this said: ""If I were there, I would show you the grave of Musa (peace be upon him) by the side of the road, near the red sand hill."
"676","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to put two men from among the martyrs of Uhud in a single garment, then he would ask, ""Which of them knew more of the Qur'an?"" When one of them was pointed out, he would put him first in the grave and say: ""I will be a witness for these people on the Day of Resurrection."" And he (peace be upon him) ordered that they be buried with their blood, and they were neither washed nor was funeral prayer offered for them."
"677","Narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out of Madinah one day and offered prayer over the martyrs of Uhud as he would offer prayer over the deceased. Then he returned and stood on the pulpit and said: ""I will precede you at the Pond (Al-Kawthar) on the Day of Resurrection and will be a witness for you. And by Allah! Indeed, at this moment I am looking at my Pond, and the keys of the treasures of the earth, or (he said:) the keys of the earth, have been given to me. By Allah! I do not fear that you will become polytheists after me, but I fear that you will compete with one another for the world."
"678","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) went with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and some other people to Ibn Sayyad, until they found him playing with some boys near the houses of Bani Maghala, and Ibn Sayyad was near the age of puberty at that time. He did not realize that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had come. Until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him with his hand. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ibn Sayyad: ""Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" Ibn Sayyad looked at him and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of the unlettered (people). After that, Ibn Sayyad said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do you bear witness that ""I am the Messenger of Allah?"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him and said: ""I believe in Allah and His Messengers."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""What do you see?"" Ibn Sayyad replied: ""A truthful one comes to me and a liar comes to me."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Your matter has been confused for you."" After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""I have kept something in my heart about you, tell me what it is?"" (The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had in mind the verse of Surah ad-Dukhan: (So watch for the Day when the sky will bring a visible smoke)). So Ibn Sayyad replied: ""It is Dukh (smoke)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You cannot go beyond your limit."" Sayyiduna Umar Farooq (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah, allow me to strike his neck. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If he is (the Dajjal), you will never be able to overpower him, and if he is not, then there is no benefit in killing him."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that after this (once again) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) went to the garden in which Ibn Sayyad was, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to hear something from Ibn Sayyad secretly before he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him in a state that he was lying wrapped in a sheet, and some murmuring sound was coming from him. Then the mother of Ibn Sayyad saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) coming, although he was hiding among the date-palm trees, so she said to Ibn Sayyad: O Saf! (and Saf was the name of Ibn Sayyad), this is Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who has come. So Ibn Sayyad sat up, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""If this woman had left him in his state, i.e., had not informed him of my coming, the reality of the matter would have become clear."
"679","Narrated Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): There was a Jewish boy who used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He became ill, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to visit him and sat by his head. Then he said to him: ""Accept Islam."" So the boy looked towards his father, who was sitting beside him. His father said to him: ""Obey Abul-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" So he accepted Islam. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, saying: ""Praise be to Allah who saved the boy from the Fire."
"680","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every child is born upon the natural disposition (fitrah) of Islam, but his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian, just as an animal gives birth to a complete and sound offspring—do you see any among them born mutilated?"" Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) would recite this verse after narrating the hadith: ""The nature upon which Allah has created mankind. There is no altering Allah's creation. That is the correct and upright religion."" (Surah Ar-Rum, Ayah: 30)"
"681","Saidna Musayyib bin Hazn (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when Abu Talib’s death approached, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him. He (peace be upon him) found Abu Jahl bin Hisham and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah bin Mughirah with him. Saidna Musayyib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Talib: “O uncle, say La ilaha illallah, so that I may testify for you before Allah.” Abu Jahl and Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah said, “O Abu Talib! Will you turn away from the way of Abdul Muttalib?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued to invite him to the testimony of faith, and they both kept repeating the same thing, until the last thing Abu Talib said was that he was on the way of Abdul Muttalib, and he refused to say La ilaha illallah (then he died). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Yes, by Allah, I will seek forgiveness for you until I am forbidden to do so.” (So he, peace be upon him, began to seek forgiveness.) Upon this, Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: “It is not befitting for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists.” (Surah At-Tawbah: 133)"
"682","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were at Baqi' graveyard with a funeral when the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came to us and sat down, and we sat around him. He had a stick in his hand, and he began to strike it on the ground. Then he said: ""For every one of you, or (he said) for every living being, his place in Paradise or Hell has been written, and it has also been written whether he is sinful or righteous."" So a man asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Should we not rely on this and stop doing deeds? Because the one whose name is written among the righteous will surely turn towards good deeds, and the one whose name is written among the sinful will go towards evil."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes! Those whose names are among the righteous will be granted the ability to do good deeds, and those who are sinful will be granted the ability to do evil."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) recited this verse: ""As for he who gives (in charity) and fears Allah and believes in the best (reward), We will ease him toward ease (i.e., Paradise)."" (Surah Al-Lail 5, 7)"
"683","Sayyiduna Thabit bin Dhahak (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever swears falsely by a religion other than Islam, for example, says, 'If such and such happened, then I am a Jew,' then he will be as he said. And whoever kills himself with a weapon, he will be punished in Hell with that same weapon."
"684","Narrated by Sayyiduna Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A man received some wounds, so he killed himself. Allah the Exalted said: 'My servant has hastened before Me (i.e., he took his own life), therefore I have made Paradise forbidden for him.'"
"685","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills himself by throttling shall keep on throttling himself in the Hellfire, and whoever kills himself with a weapon shall keep on injuring himself with it in the Hellfire."
"686","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): People passed by with a funeral, and the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) praised the deceased. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" Then another funeral passed by, and they spoke ill of the deceased. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It has become obligatory."" So Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""What has become obligatory?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Paradise has become obligatory for the one whom you praised, and Hell has become obligatory for the one whom you spoke ill of. You are Allah's witnesses on earth."
"687","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If four people testify to the goodness of a Muslim, Allah will admit him to Paradise."" We asked, ""And if three people testify to his goodness?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""And if three people testify to his goodness, (he will also enter Paradise)."" Then we asked, ""And if two people testify to his goodness?"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""And if two people (testify to his goodness, he will also enter Paradise)."" Then we did not ask the Prophet (peace be upon him) about the testimony of one person."
"688","Narrated by Sayyiduna Bara’ bin Azib from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When a believer is made to sit up in his grave and his angels come to him, then he bears witness that there is no deity except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. Thus, what Allah the Exalted has said (in Surah Ibrahim, verse 27): ‘Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word, in the life of this world and in the Hereafter,’ this is what it means.”"
"689","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked into the well where the slain polytheists of Badr were lying dead and said: ""Have you found true what your Lord promised you?"" It was said to him: ""Are you calling out to the dead?"" So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You do not hear better than they do, but they cannot respond."
"690","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: (regarding the slain of Badr) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said this: “They now know that what I used to tell them was true.” And indeed Allah the Exalted has said: “O Prophet! You cannot make the dead hear.” (Surah An-Naml: 80)."
"691","Lady Asma bint Abi Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with her) says that (on one occasion) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon, and he mentioned the trial of the grave by which a person will be tested. Upon hearing this, the Muslims cried out loudly and wept."
"692","Narrated Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him): One day after sunset, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came out and heard a (terrifying) sound. He said: ""The Jews are being punished in their graves."
"693","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave, and from the punishment of Hell, and from the trials of life and death, and from the evil of the Antichrist (Masih ad-Dajjal)."
"694","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any one of you dies, his place is shown to him every morning and evening. If he is among the people of Paradise, then from the places of Paradise, and if he is among the people of Hell, then from the places of Hell. Then it is said to him: When Allah, the Exalted, will resurrect you on the Day of Resurrection, this will be your place (in which you will enter)."
"695","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him), the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), passed away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A wet nurse has been appointed for him in Paradise."
"696","Narrated Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists (if they die before reaching puberty, will they go to Paradise or Hell?). He (peace be upon him) replied: ""Allah knows best, from the moment He created them, how they would have acted (if they had lived)—whether they are deserving of Paradise or Hell."
"697","Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would finish the Fajr prayer, he would turn towards us and say: “If any of you has seen a dream during the night, let him relate it.” Sayyiduna Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if anyone had seen a dream, he would narrate it, and then whatever Allah willed, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would interpret it. According to this practice, one day the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked us: “Has any of you seen a dream?” We replied, “No.” So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “But I saw a dream last night in which two men came to me, took hold of my hand, and led me to a sacred land. Suddenly, I saw there a man sitting and another man standing with an iron hook in his hand. He would insert it into the mouth of the sitting man until it reached the back of his neck, tearing one side of his jaw. Then he would do the same to the other side, and while he was doing this, the first side would heal. Then he would repeat it again. I asked, ‘What is this?’ The two men replied, ‘Move on.’ We moved on until we reached a man lying flat on his back, and another man was standing at his head with a small or large stone in his hand. He would crush the head of the man lying down with the stone. When he struck him and the stone rolled away, he would go and pick it up, and by the time he returned to the man, his head would have healed and returned to its original state. Then he would strike him again. I asked, ‘What is this?’ The two men said, ‘Move on.’ So we moved on until we passed by a pit like a furnace, its mouth narrow and its bottom wide. There was a fire burning in it, and inside were naked men and women. When the fire blazed up, they would rise up until they almost came out. I asked, ‘What is this?’ The two men said, ‘Move on.’ So we moved on until we reached a river of blood, in the middle of which was a man, and on the bank of the river was another man with some stones in front of him. He was standing in front of the man in the river. Whenever the man in the river tried to come out, the other man would throw a stone at his mouth and force him back to where he was. I asked, ‘What is this?’ The two men said, ‘Move on.’ So we moved on until we reached a lush, green garden. In it was a large tree, and at its root was an old man and some children sitting. Suddenly, I saw another man near the tree, in front of whom was a fire, and he was kindling it. Then the two men took me up the tree. Inside the tree was a house, and I was made to enter it. I had never seen a house more beautiful and splendid than it. In that house were some old men, some young men, some women, and some children. Then the two men took me out of that house and made me climb another branch of the tree. In it was also a house, and I was made to enter it. This house was also very beautiful and splendid. In it were some old and young men. When I had seen all this, I asked the two men, ‘You have made me wander all night, now tell me the reality of what I have seen.’ They replied, ‘Yes, we will tell you. The man whose jaw you saw being torn apart is a liar, who used to tell lies in the world, and his lies would be carried further until they spread throughout the world. So he will be treated like this until the Day of Resurrection. The man whose head you saw being crushed is the one to whom Allah gave knowledge of the Qur’an, but he would sleep neglectfully at night and not act upon it during the day. So he will be treated like this until the Day of Resurrection. The people you saw in the pit are adulterers. The man you saw in the river is a usurer. The old man sitting at the root of the tree was Ibrahim (peace be upon him), and the children around him are the children of people who died before reaching puberty. The man kindling the fire is Malik, the keeper of Hell. The first house you entered is the house of common Muslims, and the second house is that of the martyrs. I am Jibreel, and this is Mikaeel. Now raise your head.’ I raised my head and suddenly saw something like a cloud above me. They said, ‘This is your place.’ I said, ‘Let me enter my place.’ They said, ‘Some of your life remains, which you have not yet completed. If you had completed it, you could have entered your place.’”"
"698","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man (Saad bin Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him) said to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): ""My mother has passed away suddenly, and I think that if she could speak, she would surely have instructed to give charity. So if I give charity on her behalf, will she receive any reward?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes."
"699","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during his illness of death would repeatedly ask, ""Where will I be today? Where will I be tomorrow?""—that is, he was waiting for the turn of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). Then, when the day of my turn came, Allah took his soul between my side and chest, and he was buried in my house."
"700","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) says that: These six people with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained pleased until his death (no one is more deserving of the caliphate than them, so choose a caliph from among them). Then he mentioned the names of these six people: Uthman, Ali, Talha, Zubair, Abdur Rahman bin Awf, and Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"701","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not speak ill of (Muslim) men, for they have already met and embraced what they have done."
